)
]

#strong[Convergent finding]: traditional swarna-bhasma is
#strong[face-centered cubic crystalline gold at the nanoscale], with no
significant gold oxide or sulfide content. The traditional procedure
produces what the texts say it should: #emph[bhasma] (ash-form) of pure
gold.

#strong[Reproducibility:] High. The procedure is standardized across
licensed Ayurvedic pharmacies. Multiple modern studies have
characterized batches from different producers and found consistent FCC
nano-gold structure.

=== 2.4 The traditional confirmation tests
<the-traditional-confirmation-tests>
Classical texts specify qualitative tests that swarna-bhasma must pass
before being considered ready for medicinal use:

#align(center)[#table(
  columns: 4,
  align: (col, row) => (auto,auto,auto,auto,).at(col),
  inset: 6pt,
  [Test], [Sanskrit], [Description], [Modern interpretation],
  [#emph[Rekhapurnatva]],
  [रेखापूर्णत्व],
  [Particles enter the furrows of the fingers when rubbed],
  [Particle size \<10 μm (skin furrow width)],
  [#emph[Varitaratva]],
  [वारितरत्व],
  [Floats on water surface],
  [Hydrophobic surface, very small particle size, surface tension can
  support particles],
  [#emph[Apunarbhava]],
  [अपुनर्भव],
  [Cannot be reverted to source metal even on heating],
  [Truly converted to bhasma form, not just temporary form],
  [#emph[Niruttha]],
  [निरुत्थ],
  [Does not regain metallic character with silver test],
  [Confirmed non-metallic state],
  [#emph[Nirdhuma]],
  [निर्धूम],
  [No smoke when heated],
  [No volatile contaminants remaining],
  [#emph[Niswadu]],
  [निःस्वादु],
  [Tasteless],
  [No ionic dissolution],
  [#emph[Nischandratva]],
  [निःचन्द्रत्व],
  [No metallic shine],
  [Particle size \<visible-light wavelength],
)
]

These tests, developed empirically over centuries, function as effective
quality control. #emph[Rekhapurnatva] directly tests for particle size
\<10 μm. #emph[Varitaratva] tests for nano/micro scale (water-floating
bhasma must have very small, hydrophobic particles). #emph[Niswadu] and
#emph[Niruttha] test for absence of ionic gold (which would taste
metallic and would react in silver test).

#strong[Convergence with modern QC:] These traditional tests
collectively measure: particle size, surface chemistry, completeness of
conversion. Modern analytical methods (XRD, SEM, ICP-OES) measure the
same things with greater precision. The traditional tests are
pre-analytical-instrument quality control that, when properly performed,
correlate well with modern validation.

