== 4. Framework Timing Predictions
<framework-timing-predictions>
=== 4.1 Methodology
<methodology>
Applying the Atlas computational framework (which achieved 91.7%
structural recovery of classical ashtadhatu nakshatra prescriptions) to
gold operations: gold is single-graha (Surya) for the primary substance,
with graha contributions from co-substances varying by procedure.

=== 4.2 Pure gold operations (shodhana, swarna-varkha preparation)
<pure-gold-operations-shodhana-swarna-varkha-preparation>
Single-graha analysis (Surya-only). Friendship from BPHS: - Surya is
friend of: Chandra (Moon), Mangala (Mars), Guru (Jupiter) - Surya is
enemy of: Shukra (Venus), Shani (Saturn) - Surya is neutral to: Budha
(Mercury), Rahu, Ketu

Framework predicts highest favorability when nakshatra-lord is friendly
to Surya: - #strong[Most favorable:] Rohini (Chandra), Mrigashira
(Mangala), Punarvasu (Guru), Hasta (Chandra), Chitra (Mangala), Vishakha
(Guru), Shravana (Chandra), Dhanishtha (Mangala), Purva Bhadrapada
(Guru) - #strong[Least favorable:] Bharani (Shukra), Pushya (Shani),
Anuradha (Shani), Purva Phalguni (Shukra), Purva Ashadha (Shukra),
Uttara Bhadrapada (Shani)

This is a notable finding: #strong[gold operations are predicted to be
unfavorable on Pushya nakshatra], despite Pushya being one of the most
generally auspicious nakshatras and a Dhruva nakshatra. This is because
Pushya is Shani-ruled, and Shani is enemy to Surya.

The framework prediction is internally consistent: classical murti
pratishtha texts list Pushya as auspicious for general murti
installation, but specific deity-murti recipes that prioritize gold
(Vishnu, Lakshmi) often specify Surya-friendly nakshatras (Rohini,
Uttara Phalguni — Surya-ruled — over Pushya).

=== 4.3 Gold-mercury operations (swarna-bhasma marana)
<gold-mercury-operations-swarna-bhasma-marana>
Two-graha (Surya + Budha). Surya is #emph[neutral] to Budha in BPHS
naisargika friendship. Framework predicts moderate favorability across
most nakshatras with neither strong preference nor strong avoidance.

The neutral friendship is significant: it means swarna-bhasma marana
operations are #emph[less timing-sensitive] than operations involving
graha pairs with strong friend/enemy relationships. This may explain why
classical texts give less specific timing prescriptions for
swarna-bhasma compared to operations like sindoor preparation (where
Budha-Mangala enemy relationship makes timing critical).

#strong[Practical implication:] swarna-bhasma can be effectively
prepared across a wider range of timing windows than substances
involving more polarized graha pairs. This matches actual practice:
pharmaceutical-grade swarna-bhasma is produced in licensed pharmacies
year-round without strict timing prescription.

=== 4.4 Gold-mercury-sulfur operations (makaradhwaja)
<gold-mercury-sulfur-operations-makaradhwaja>
Three-graha (Surya + Budha + Mangala). Surya friendly to Mangala; Surya
neutral to Budha; Budha enemy to Mangala (the tension noted in Volume I
§5.3).

Framework predicts: - #strong[Most favorable:] Pushya (Shani-ruled —
neutral to all three primary grahas of operation, Dhruva activity-class)
— #emph[despite] Shani being enemy of Surya, the dominant factor for the
three-graha integration is which nakshatra-lord doesn’t strongly oppose
any of them - #strong[Strong secondary:] Anuradha (Shani-ruled), Uttara
Bhadrapada (Shani-ruled) — same logic - #strong[Avoid:] Ashlesha
(Budha-ruled, amplifies Mercury but tension with Mars increases)

This prediction parallels the Volume I finding for kajjali preparation.
The Pushya nakshatra emerges as a stable timing point for multi-graha
mercurial operations precisely because Shani’s overall neutrality serves
as a coherent backdrop for complex multi-graha integration.

=== 4.5 Gold-silver operations (swarna-tara or in panchaloha context)
<gold-silver-operations-swarna-tara-or-in-panchaloha-context>
Two-graha (Surya + Chandra). Surya is friend of Chandra. #emph[Both
directions of friendship] — this is one of the most stable graha pairs
in the BPHS framework.

Framework predicts strong favorability across many nakshatras: -
#strong[Most favorable:] Rohini (Chandra-ruled, Chandra most receptive
to Surya), Hasta (Chandra), Shravana (Chandra), Krittika (Surya-ruled,
Surya stable), Uttara Phalguni (Surya), Uttara Ashadha (Surya) -
#strong[Avoid:] Bharani, Purva Phalguni, Purva Ashadha (Shukra-ruled —
Shukra enemy of Surya)

The Surya-Chandra harmony is structurally responsible for why panchaloha
and ashtadhatu (which include both gold and silver as components) have
such broad sets of favorable nakshatras.

=== 4.6 Pure gold leaf preparation specifically
<pure-gold-leaf-preparation-specifically>
The mechanical work of beating gold into leaf (#emph[swarna-varkha])
involves only the gold itself; the framework prediction is purely
Surya-centered. However, since leaf preparation is a multi-day process,
the framework’s timing prediction would emphasize stable Surya-friendly
conditions throughout the process duration rather than a single peak
moment.

This suggests an extended prediction model (forward-time-integration)
would be valuable for procedures with non-trivial duration. Such a model
is noted in the "Future Work" section as a separate development.

