== 5. Gap Analysis: Tradition vs Modern Interpretation
<gap-analysis-tradition-vs-modern-interpretation>
=== 5.1 Where the tradition is correct
<where-the-tradition-is-correct>
- #strong[Gold is biologically inert] — accurately observed; gold is one
  of the safest metals for human exposure
- #strong[Particle size matters] — accurately observed via
  #emph[rekhapurnatva], #emph[varitaratva], #emph[nischandratva] tests;
  modern characterization confirms nano-scale dimensions
- #strong[Heating-cooling cycles refine the metal] — accurately
  observed; thermomechanical processing is exactly what these cycles
  accomplish
- #strong[Final preparation should not regain metallic character] —
  accurately observed; #emph[apunarbhava] and #emph[niruttha] tests
  verify completion
- #strong[Gold has medhya (cognitive) and rasayana (rejuvenating)
  properties] — partially supported; gold compounds have established
  anti-inflammatory effects, gold nanoparticles in modern research show
  various therapeutic applications
- #strong[Gold-based preparations should be prepared with mercury and
  sulfur as co-mediators] — supported; this is essentially a
  citrate-reduction-equivalent synthesis pathway producing nano-gold

=== 5.2 Where the tradition’s claims need qualification
<where-the-traditions-claims-need-qualification>
- #strong["Gold removes all diseases"] — overstatement; gold has
  specific therapeutic applications, not panacea status
- #strong["Sahaja Swarna" (cosmic-origin gold)] — this is
  mythological/symbolic, not a chemically distinct grade
- #strong["Rasaja Swarna" (alchemical gold from base metals)] — not
  validated chemistry; refers to gilding-type processes (see Volume I
  §2.4.8)
- #strong[Specific weight-conservation claims in gold-mercury jarana] —
  not validated by modern reproduction (see Volume I §2.4.3)
- #strong[Some specific clinical efficacy claims] — under-investigated;
  would benefit from modern controlled trials

=== 5.3 Where the framework can help
<where-the-framework-can-help>
- #strong[Identifying which gold operations have strong vs. weak timing
  dependence] — Surya-Chandra integration (panchaloha) has strong
  predictions; pure swarna-bhasma less so
- #strong[Predicting which nakshatras to avoid for gold-specific
