  swarna-bhasma specifically

=== 5.4 The empirical convergence finding
<the-empirical-convergence-finding>
Of all dhatus, gold shows the strongest empirical convergence between
classical claim and modern characterization. The texts said: - Pure gold
reduced to fine ash form (#emph[bhasma]) - Particles small enough to
enter finger furrows (≤10 μm) - Surface tension permits floating on
water (sub-micron features) - No metallic shine when finely powdered
(sub-wavelength features) - Cannot be reverted to bulk gold by simple
heating (genuinely transformed)

Modern characterization confirms: - ≥95% pure Au, FCC crystalline -
Particle size 5-57 nm depending on method (well below 10 μm) -
Sub-micron features confirmed by SEM - Sub-wavelength features confirmed
by TEM - Bhasma form is stable; elemental gold can be recovered only by
re-melting with strong reducing agents

#strong[The classical procedure produces what the texts said it would
produce], characterized at the empirical limits modern instruments
allow. This is the cleanest case of tradition-modern convergence in the
entire compendium.

