== 9. Closing Notes
<closing-notes>
Gold is the volume where modern characterization most strongly validates
classical preparation methods. The texts said #emph[swarna-bhasma] is
finely-divided ash-form gold; modern XRD/TEM/SEM confirms FCC
crystalline gold nanoparticles in the 5-57 nm range. The convergence is
striking enough that gold-bhasma chemistry deserves serious attention
from both Ayurvedic and contemporary nanomedicine research communities.

The framework’s contribution to gold-specific work is more nuanced than
for mercury. Where mercury required us to distinguish reproducible
chemistry from aspirational claim, gold lets us study which timing
windows might affect quality parameters (particle size distribution,
crystallographic perfection) of a substance whose basic chemistry is
already well-established and reproducible. The framework predictions
become testable hypotheses about variance within a settled production
paradigm rather than questions about whether a substance is what it’s
claimed to be.

The Pushya-nakshatra finding deserves attention: framework predicts that
pure gold operations are #emph[less] favorable on Pushya despite
Pushya’s general auspiciousness, due to Shani-Surya enmity. This is the
kind of specific, framework-derived prediction that would be
straightforward to test in a retrospective study of licensed-pharmacy
swarna-bhasma quality records.

